sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: Cloud gaming with Realtime SFU
  accDescr: An authenticated browser uses a Worker and GameContainer Durable Object for application state. A Container publishes media through Realtime SFU, and one controlling browser sends input replies through two DataChannels.

  participant Browser as Browser tab
  box rgb(251, 227, 207) Application boundary
    participant Worker as Worker
    participant Game as Game state
  end
  participant SFU as Realtime SFU
  participant Container as Container publisher

  Note over Browser,Game: Access identity + per-tab capability<br/>One SFU session and PeerConnection per browser tab
  Browser->>Worker: App request
  Worker->>Game: Typed RPC
  Game->>Container: Start or stop
  Container->>Game: Register publisher
  Game->>SFU: Create SFU resources

  Container->>SFU: Publish H.264 + Opus
  Container->>SFU: Publish two input channels
  SFU-->>Browser: Subscribe to media + channels
  Game->>SFU: Enable controller replies
  Browser->>SFU: Reliable keyboard + buttons
  Browser->>SFU: Replaceable pointer movement
  SFU-->>Container: Forward controller input
